"program_narrative": "Program PORTVALD is a called validation subroutine (PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LS-VALIDATION-REQUEST) that checks one portfolio data element per call. The caller sets LS-VALIDATE-TYPE and LS-INPUT-VALUE; the program validates a portfolio ID (I: must start with 'PORT' followed by numeric digits), an account number (A: numeric and not zero), an investment type (T: one of STK, BND, MMF, ETF) or an amount (M: within the VAL-MIN-AMOUNT..VAL-MAX-AMOUNT range). It uses no files or tables; constants, messages and work areas come from copybook PORTVAL. The result is returned in LS-RETURN-CODE (VAL-SUCCESS 0, or VAL-INVALID-ID/ACCT/TYPE/AMT 1-4) with an error message in LS-ERROR-MSG. Error conditions handled: an unknown validation type returns VAL-INVALID-ID with 'Invalid validation type'; each failed check returns its specific code and message and leaves the paragraph early. Static review notes: the portfolio-ID numeric check and the account-number numeric check are flagged in trace_issues because, as written, they reject values that the comments describe as valid.",
